  "limitations": [
    "M3 panels, physical millimetre shift views and viewport overlays are not implemented",
    "Headless evidence does not establish GNOME/Wayland, accessibility or human workflow acceptance",
    "Enabled GPU rendering is explicitly rejected; M1 HIP evidence does not validate changed native kernel data",
    "Motion blur, motion-vector passes, stereo/multiview, non-perspective cameras and adaptive subdivision are explicitly rejected",
    "Finite manual native focus only; exact positive-infinite focus is numerical-helper evidence",
    "Radiometry uses Cycles exposure-normalized aperture sampling, with binary angular coverage and no calibrated physical throughput or falloff",
    "Generic camera-position/distance coordinates retain body-anchor semantics; baking has no acceptance evidence",
    "Shader transforms describe the chief projection, not a unique inverse of finite-aperture blur",
    "Fixtures cover a bounded static CPU set, not arbitrary production scenes or real-lens accuracy"
  ],
